#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:9
msgid "Remove the Direct-DOM Path"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:13
msgid "`VTKJSRenderer` has two render modes selected by `use_ipython`. The IPython path generates vtk.js JavaScript and displays it through `display(Javascript(...))`. The direct-DOM path (reached in Pyodide without IPython) exists but is incomplete: `create_container()` builds a `<div>` without creating any vtk.js objects for it, and `render()` calls `self.renderer.resetCamera()` and `self.render_window.render()` on attributes that pyvista-js never sets — the code even carries `# type: ignore[attr-defined]` comments on both lines (`src/pyvista_js/rendering.py`, lines 1264–1265). Calling `render()` in that mode therefore raises `AttributeError`. The bug was found while improving test coverage in [pyvista-js#776](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-js/pull/776) and reported in [pyvista-js#778](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-js/issues/778): should the direct-DOM path be implemented properly, or removed?"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:15
msgid "Review of this record noted that no current demo reaches the direct-DOM path. JupyterLite's Pyodide kernel includes IPython, so it takes the IPython path; the Streamlit demo renders with `generate_standalone_html()` and never calls `VTKJSRenderer.render()`; and the `stlite/` directory named in the contributing instructions is stale and absent from `main`. A concrete non-IPython use case (for example, a PyScript page embedding Pyodide without IPython) therefore remains hypothetical."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:17
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:19
msgid "**You aren't gonna need it (YAGNI)**: capability for an embedding with no current user should not be built; the unused direct-DOM path and any new code serving only hypothetical configurations should be deleted rather than extended."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:20
msgid "**Correctness over dead code**: A code path that always raises `AttributeError` when reached is a defect, and the `type: ignore` annotations hide it from both mypy and readers."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:21
msgid "**Reachability of a plausible target**: no current demo reaches the direct-DOM path, but Pyodide without IPython (for example, a PyScript page) is a plausible future embedding, and a path that always crashes there gives no clear error for that configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:22
msgid "**Testability**: Coverage tooling flags the branch, and the maintainers want the suite to cover it either way — a tested implementation is also the natural target of the existing Playwright tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:23
msgid "**Maintenance cost**: Implementing direct-DOM rendering means creating and wiring the full vtk.js object graph (`render_window`, `renderer`, context) from Python in `src/pyvista_js/rendering.py`, duplicating logic that today lives in the vtk.js wiring of `ts/renderer.ts` and is embedded into the generated JavaScript of the IPython path."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:24
msgid "**Time to a safe release**: the crash defect should disappear from released pyvista-js soon; options that require substantial new implementation and testing delay that release."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:25
msgid "**Loud and helpful failure**: a configuration that cannot render should fail with an explicit, informative message suggesting a working alternative, instead of crashing or silently doing nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:27
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:29
msgid "Implement the direct-DOM path: make `create_container()` create the vtk.js object graph and `render()` drive it."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:30
msgid "Remove the direct-DOM path: make the non-IPython branch raise an explicit, informative error."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:31
msgid "Keep the path but document it as experimental and guard `render()` so it degrades gracefully instead of crashing."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:32
msgid "Replay the generated JavaScript in non-IPython pages: run the existing `_generate_render_js()` output of the IPython path inside the page instead of rebuilding the vtk.js object graph from Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:33
msgid "Share a single TypeScript render entry point: refactor `ts/renderer.ts` so both the IPython path and the direct-DOM path drive rendering through one entry function, with Python passing the rendering data and the container element."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:35
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:37
msgid "Chosen option: \"Remove the direct-DOM path\", because YAGNI ranks first and removal is the only option that is Good under it: with no current demo reaching the direct-DOM path and no concrete non-IPython use case, building — or replaying — rendering capability for a hypothetical embedding is exactly the speculative work YAGNI rules out. Review of this record and discussion with larsoner in [pyvista-js#797](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-js/pull/797) settled removal, and the ranking agrees. The decision is revisitable: a concrete non-IPython use case (for example, a PyScript page embedding Pyodide without IPython) triggers a new record, where replaying the existing `_generate_render_js()` output inside the container `create_container()` builds — rather than rebuilding the vtk.js object graph from Python — is the recorded starting point because it avoids a second wiring that must stay in sync with `ts/renderer.ts`."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:39
msgid "The scope of the removal reaches beyond `render()`. `get_renderer()` still selects `VTKJSRenderer` in Pyodide without IPython, and `VTKJSRenderer.__init__`, `create_container()`, `clear()`, and `_VTKJSLoader` all carry code that serves only the direct-DOM path. Raising the explicit error in `__init__` (or not selecting `VTKJSRenderer` in `get_renderer()`) and deleting those branches removes the path cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:41
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:43
msgid "Good, because it deletes the unused branch instead of building for hypothetical users, which is what the first-ranked driver YAGNI calls for."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:44
#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:73
msgid "Good, because it replaces the `AttributeError` with a loud, intentional error and removes the masked dead path and its `type: ignore` comments."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:45
#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:75
msgid "Neutral, because the exposed failure is deterministic and easy to test, and the Playwright surface neither shrinks nor grows."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:46
#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:76
msgid "Good, because it is the smallest change, with no duplicated vtk.js wiring to maintain."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:47
#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:77
msgid "Good, because a small Python-side change can ship the fix quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:48
#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:78
msgid "Good, because the exposed error carries guidance, such as installing IPython or using `generate_standalone_html()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:50
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:52
msgid "Confirmed by a unit test that calls `create_container()` and `render()` in Pyodide without IPython and without preset `renderer`/`render_window` attributes and asserts the explicit error with alternative guidance (note that `tests/test_rendering.py::test_render_loads_vtkjs_in_pyodide` cannot serve as this check because it injects stand-ins for both attributes, so it passes with the defect still present). Accepted after discussion in [tkoyama010/pyvista-js#797](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-js/pull/797)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:54
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:56
msgid "Implement the direct-DOM path"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:58
msgid "At `create_container()` time, construct the vtk.js object graph for the container; `render()` then calls `resetCamera()` and `render_window.render()` on real objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:60
msgid "Bad, because wiring the full vtk.js object graph builds speculative capability for an embedding no current demo reaches."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:61
msgid "Good, because it removes the guaranteed `AttributeError` defect, and the `type: ignore[attr-defined]` markers that mask it can be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:62
msgid "Good, because a possible Pyodide-without-IPython embedding gets real rendering instead of a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:63
msgid "Good, because the direct-DOM branch becomes reachable and testable by tests that exercise the real lifecycle rather than injected stand-ins."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:64
msgid "Neutral, because a second vtk.js object wiring path now exists alongside the generated-JavaScript IPython path, and the two must be kept in sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:65
msgid "Bad, because the fix waits on new vtk.js wiring plus new unit and browser tests before it can ship."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:66
msgid "Neutral, because a completed implementation leaves no unsupported configuration to fail, but until it lands the crash stays."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:68
msgid "Remove the direct-DOM path (accepted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:70
msgid "Raise an explicit `RuntimeError` with guidance (for example, \"install or initialize IPython, or use `generate_standalone_html()`\") when not in IPython."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:72
msgid "Good, because it deletes the unused branch instead of building for hypothetical users."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:74
msgid "Bad, because Pyodide-without-IPython becomes a permanently unsupported configuration, with `VTKJSRenderer` degrading to IPython-only despite accepting that environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:80
msgid "Keep the path but document it as experimental"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:82
msgid "Keep the path untouched but catch `AttributeError` and warn."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:84
msgid "Bad, because it keeps an unused branch around instead of deleting it."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:85
msgid "Bad, because the masked defect and the `type: ignore[attr-defined]` comments stay, and a caught `AttributeError` turns the crash into a silent no-op, which is worse than a clear error."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:86
msgid "Bad, because in Pyodide without IPython the scene still does not render, so the supported use case gets no visualization."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:87
msgid "Good, because the guarded branch becomes deterministic and testable, and a no-IPython test needs no stand-ins for `renderer` or `render_window`."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:88
msgid "Good, because the implementation work is near zero: no vtk.js wiring is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:89
msgid "Neutral, because the catch-and-warn guard is a small change, but it leaves the rendering question unresolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:90
msgid "Bad, because the guarded branch still renders nothing and only prints a warning instead of informative guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:92
msgid "Replay the generated JavaScript in non-IPython pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:94
msgid "Make the non-IPython branch emit the same JavaScript the IPython path generates through `_generate_render_js()` and inject it into the container built by `create_container()`, reusing the single vtk.js object wiring that lives in `ts/renderer.ts`."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:96
msgid "Bad, because, like implementing the path, it adds rendering capability for an embedding no current demo reaches, only at smaller cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:97
#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:109
msgid "Good, because it removes the guaranteed `AttributeError` defect with a deliberate behavior instead of a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:98
msgid "Good, because a possible non-IPython embedding gets real rendering drawn by the same code as the IPython path."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:99
msgid "Neutral, because the generated JavaScript is written for the IPython display context, so standalone execution must first be proven by a browser test."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:100
msgid "Good, because nothing new must stay in sync with `ts/renderer.ts`, at the bounded cost of `create_container()` still placing a suitable host element."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:101
msgid "Good, because only Python-side changes are needed, with no TypeScript rebuild in the loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:102
msgid "Neutral, because if the replayed output fails in the browser, the failure carries no informative message."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:104
msgid "Share a single TypeScript render entry point"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:106
msgid "Refactor `ts/renderer.ts` so the IPython path and the direct-DOM path drive rendering through the same entry function; Python passes the rendering data and the container element, and the bundle creates the vtk.js object graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:108
msgid "Bad, because it refactors the bundle to serve an embedding no current demo reaches."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:110
msgid "Good, because a possible Pyodide-without-IPython embedding gets real rendering."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:111
msgid "Good, because both modes exercise the same tested code, so one browser test covers the shared entry point."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:112
msgid "Good, because a single vtk.js wiring remains: there is no second object graph to keep in sync, at only the one-time cost of refactoring the entry function out of `ts/renderer.ts` and rebuilding the bundle."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:113
msgid "Bad, because the fix waits on the TypeScript refactor, rebuild, and new tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:114
msgid "Neutral, because a completed shared entry point leaves no unsupported configuration to fail, but until it lands the crash stays."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:116
msgid "More Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:118
msgid "Issue: [tkoyama010/pyvista-js#778](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-js/issues/778)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:119
msgid "Coverage PR that surfaced it: [tkoyama010/pyvista-js#776](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-js/pull/776)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:120
msgid "Review discussion of this record: [tkoyama010/pyvista-js#797](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-js/pull/797)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0003-remove-the-direct-dom-path.md:121
msgid "Affected code: `src/pyvista_js/rendering.py`, `VTKJSRenderer.__init__`, `VTKJSRenderer.create_container`, `VTKJSRenderer.render`, `VTKJSRenderer.clear`, `_VTKJSLoader`, and the `get_renderer` selection of `VTKJSRenderer`"
msgstr ""

